   "payload": {
    "report_excerpt": "Based on my research, I found a real domain availability API service. Let me report my findings.\n\nHere is a real domain availability API service I found:\n\n**GoDaddy Domains API v3**\n\nName: GoDaddy Domains API (Discovery/Availability Endpoint)\nURL: https://developer.godaddy.com/doc/endpoint/domains\n\nThe GoDaddy Domains v3 API is a REST API that provides domain availability checking. Key endpoints include:\n\n- GET /v3/domains/suggestions - Suggest available domains for a query\n- GET /v3/domains/availability - Check if specific domains are available\n\nThe API uses Bearer token authentication (Personal Access Token) and returns JSON responses indicating whether a domain is available, taken, or available for purchase.\n\nBase URL: https://api.godaddy.com/v3/domains\n\nAdditionally, WhoisXML API (https://www.whoisxmlapi.com/) is another service that offers a Domain Availability API as part of their broader domain intelligence platform, though their specific documentation pages were returning 404 errors during my investigation.",
    "named_urls": [
     "https://developer.godaddy.com/doc/endpoint/domains",
